# Stage 4: AI Health Intelligence & Backend Validation

This stage focuses on transforming SportApp into a "Pro" wellness assistant by leveraging AI to analyze user performance and securing the backend against malicious or malformed data.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gemini Usage**: This feature will use the Gemini API key provided by the user in settings. If no key is provided, the AI report will show a placeholder or prompt the user.
> [!NOTE]
> **Input Validation**: We will introduce `express-validator`. This means any API calls with incorrect data types (e.g., text in weight field) will be strictly rejected with 400 Bad Request.

## Proposed Changes

### 🛡️ Backend Security (Hardening Part 2)

#### [MODIFY] [auth.js](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/routes/auth.js), [sync.js](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/routes/sync.js)
- Add `express-validator` middleware to check types, lengths, and formats for all incoming data (weights, tasks, notes, etc.).

### 🤖 AI Health Intelligence

#### [NEW] [ai_coach.js](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/routes/ai_coach.js)
- Create a new router for AI-driven insights.
- **Endpoint**: `GET /api/ai/weekly-summary`
- **Logic**: 
  - Fetch user's data for the last 7 days.
  - Construct a detailed prompt for Gemini (Markdown formatted).
  - Return a professional "Coach's Report".

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/server.js)
- Mount the new `/api/ai` route.

### 🌐 Web & Mobile Frontend

#### [MODIFY] [app.js](file:///c:/projects/SportApp/public/app.js) & [Mobile Dashboard]
- Add an "AI Coach Summary" card to the dashboard.
- Display a "Generating..." shimmer while the report is being calculated.

